-- title:
--   Drinfeld chart of the completed stalk at a supersingular point
-- statement:
--   **Arithmetic data.** Let $q$ be a prime and $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$ (`hqM'`). Let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ (`hℓ12`) and $\ell \mid M'$ (`hℓM'`). Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $q\ell$, let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $q$-th root of unity, $\xi \in L$ a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity, and assume $\zeta = \xi^{\ell}$ (`hζξ`). Let $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^{\times}$ be the subgroup equal (`hH₁`) to the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^{\times} \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^{\times}$, with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^{\times} \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^{\times}$ coming from $\ell \mid q^2M'$; thus $H_1$ consists of the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$ and modulo $\ell$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((T))$ equal (`hK`) to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is, the $L$-subfield of $L((T))$ generated by the coefficientwise image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the $q$-expansion function field of $X_{H_1}$ at level $q^2M'$ over $\mathbb{Q}$.
--
--   **The base ring and the $j$-line.** Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with an $L$-algebra structure making $L$ its fraction field, such that $q$ lies in the maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hAq`) and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$ (`hζA`), equipped with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with that of $L$ (`IsScalarTower A L ↥K`). Let $j \in K$ be the element whose Laurent series is [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), the $q$-expansion of the modular $j$-function (`hj`), assumed nonzero as a `Fact`, and let $\varpi$ generate $\mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hϖ`).
--
--   Write $\mathfrak{X} =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A (↥K) j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) for the two-chart integral model of $K$ over $A$ relative to $j$: the pushout glueing $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the finite chart algebra `chartAlgFin A (↥K) j`, the subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, with $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the chart at infinity; `toBase` denotes its structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} A$, `ιFin` the morphism from the finite chart $\mathrm{XFin} = \operatorname{Spec}(\mathrm{chartAlgFin})$, and `jChartFin` the element $j$ viewed inside the finite chart algebra.
--
--   **The point.** Let $z$ be a point of $\mathfrak{X}$, and let $\varpi_z$ be the germ at $z$ of the global section of $\mathfrak{X}$ obtained from $\varpi$ along `toBase` (`hϖz`), assumed to lie in the maximal ideal of the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{\mathfrak{X},z}$ (`hz`), so that $z$ lies in the special fibre. Let $y$ be a point of $\mathrm{XFin}$ with `ιFin` sending $y$ to $z$ (`hy`). The supersingularity hypothesis `hss` requires: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ with decidable equality and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the finite chart algebra to $\Omega$ whose kernel is the prime $y$, the value $\varphi(\mathrm{jChartFin})$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of those $\bar{j} \in \Omega$ such that every elliptic curve $W/\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $\bar{j}$ has no nonzero point killed by $q$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Under these hypotheses there exist: a complete discrete valuation domain $W$ (a commutative ring which is a domain, a discrete valuation ring, and adically complete for its maximal ideal), a ring homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ with $\mathfrak{m}_W = (\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f, u, v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u$ and $v$ units and
--   $$f - \big(X_0X_1^{\,q} - X_0^{\,q}X_1\big) \in (X_0,X_1)^{q+2},$$
--   the subtracted term being [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18), and a ring isomorphism
--   $$e : \widehat{\mathcal{O}}_{\mathfrak{X},z} \;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\; S := W[[X_0,X_1]]\big/\big(C(\sigma\varpi)\,v - f\,u\big),$$
--   where $\widehat{\mathcal{O}}_{\mathfrak{X},z}$ is the adic completion of the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{\mathfrak{X},z}$ with respect to its maximal ideal, such that the following six assertions hold. Throughout, `toC` denotes the canonical map $\mathcal{O}_{\mathfrak{X},z} \to \widehat{\mathcal{O}}_{\mathfrak{X},z}$, `mkS` the quotient map $W[[X_0,X_1]] \to S$, and `germY` the ring homomorphism from the finite chart algebra to $\mathcal{O}_{\mathfrak{X},z}$ given by the germ at $z$ of sections over the open image of `ιFin`, identified with the chart algebra.
--
--   (i) *Compatibility with the base.* For every $a \in A$, the image under $e \circ \mathrm{toC}$ of the germ at $z$ of $a$ pulled back along `toBase` equals $\mathrm{mkS}(C(\sigma a))$.
--
--   (ii) *Stability of the finite chart.* For every $\gamma \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ lying in $\Gamma_0(M')$ and every $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ satisfying [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) — that is, for all weights $k$, all modular forms $f_0, g_0$ for $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ of weight $k$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f, p_g$ and $g_0 \neq 0$ in the relevant sense, all $x \in K$ whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of $p_f/p_g$, and all embeddings $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota\zeta = e^{2\pi i/q}$, one has $\iota(\tau x)\cdot (g_0\mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1})^{\wedge} = (f_0\mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1})^{\wedge}$ as $q$-expansions — the automorphism $\tau$ maps the finite chart algebra into itself.
--
--   (iii) *Triviality on the residue at $y$ for $\ell$-trivial $\gamma$.* For every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod{\ell}$, every $\tau$ as in (ii) for $\gamma^{-1}$, and every proof that $\tau$ preserves the finite chart algebra, the induced endomorphism of the chart algebra satisfies $\tau(a) - a \in y$ for all $a$ in the chart algebra.
--
--   (iv) *Linearisation of the level automorphisms.* For every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, every $\tau$ with `IsLevelAutAt` for $\gamma^{-1}$ as in (ii), every proof `hpres` that $\tau$ preserves the finite chart algebra, and under the further assumption that $\tau(a) - a \in y$ for all $a$ in the chart algebra, there exist a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c \in W$ and a matrix $M \in \mathrm{Mat}_2(W)$ such that: $\theta$ intertwines $\tau$ with itself through $e \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY}$, i.e. $\theta(e(\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}\,a))) = e(\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}(\tau a)))$ for all $a$ in the chart algebra; $\theta$ fixes every constant $\mathrm{mkS}(C\,w)$, $w \in W$; for each index $j'$, $\theta(\mathrm{mkS}(X_{j'})) - \mathrm{mkS}\big(\sum_{i} C(M_{i j'})X_i\big)$ lies in the square of the ideal of $S$ generated by $\mathrm{mkS}(X_0), \mathrm{mkS}(X_1)$; $c^{q+1} - 1 \in \mathfrak{m}_W$; $M_{ij} \equiv c\,\gamma_{ij} \pmod{\mathfrak{m}_W}$ for all $i,j$; if $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod{\ell}$ then $c \equiv 1 \pmod{\mathfrak{m}_W}$; and if $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity on $K$, then $c - 1 \notin \mathfrak{m}_W$.
--
--   (v) *Distinctness of branches with independent tangents.* For all integers $a_1, b_1, a_2, b_2$ and all prime ideals $P_1, P_2$ of $S$ such that each $P_i$ fails to contain at least one of $\mathrm{mkS}(X_0), \mathrm{mkS}(X_1)$, each contains $\mathrm{mkS}(C(\sigma\varpi))$, and for each $i$ there is $h \in (X_0,X_1)^2 \subseteq W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $\mathrm{mkS}\big(C(a_i)X_0 + C(b_i)X_1 + h\big) \in P_i$, if $q \nmid a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$ then the contractions of $P_1$ and $P_2$ to $\mathcal{O}_{\mathfrak{X},z}$ along $e \circ \mathrm{toC}$ are distinct ideals.
--
--   (vi) *Identification of the branch with tangent $X_0$.* For every prime ideal $P$ of $S$ which fails to contain at least one of $\mathrm{mkS}(X_0), \mathrm{mkS}(X_1)$, contains $\mathrm{mkS}(C(\sigma\varpi))$, and for which there is $h \in (X_0,X_1)^2$ with $\mathrm{mkS}\big(C(1)X_0 + C(0)X_1 + h\big) \in P$, and for every $a$ in the finite chart algebra: $\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}\,a)$ lies in the contraction of $P$ along $e$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$, viewed in $L((T))$, lies in the image of $\mathfrak{m}_A$ under $A \to L$, i.e. for every $n \in \mathbb{Z}$ there is $m \in \mathfrak{m}_A$ with $\mathrm{coeff}_n(a) =$ the image of $m$.
--
--   This is the local Drinfeld chart at a supersingular point in residue characteristic $q$: the completed local ring of the integral model of the full-level modular curve attached to $H_1$ is presented as $W[[X_0,X_1]]/(\varpi v - fu)$ with $f$ congruent to Drinfeld's form $X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ modulo degree $q+2$, together with the $\Gamma_0(M')$-equivariance of the presentation, the mod-$\mathfrak{m}_W$ linearisation of the level automorphisms, and a description of the branches through the point. It is the variant rigidified by a $\Gamma_1$-structure at a guard prime $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$, with constants $\mathbb{Q}(\xi) = \mathbb{Q}(\zeta_{q\ell})$, so that no lower bound on $q$ is required; it feeds [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_stalk_drinfeldChart_of_mem_ssJSet_of_pow_eq_mul_moduliHasse_of_isPrimitiveRoot_mul_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_stalk_drinfeldChart_of_mem_ssJSet_of_pow_eq_mul_moduliHasse_of_isPrimitiveRoot_mul_of_dvd).
